---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro'
import Callout from 'web-design-system/astro/marketing/Callout.astro'
import CodeBlock from 'web-design-system/astro/product/CodeBlock.astro'
import TableScroll from '../../components/TableScroll.astro'
import { Badge } from 'web-design-system/components'

const toc = [
  { label: 'In-app settings', href: '#settings' },
  { label: 'Agent providers and models', href: '#agent' },
  { label: 'Todoist', href: '#todoist' },
  { label: 'GitHub', href: '#github' },
  { label: 'Going deeper', href: '#deeper' },
]

const config = `{
  "provider": "auto",
  "model": "auto",
  "max_turns": 50,

  "providers": {
    "openrouter": {
      "base_url": "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1",
      "api_key": "env:OPENROUTER_API_KEY",
      "models": ["openrouter/free"]
    }
  },

  "combos": {
    "coding": [
      ["poolside", "poolside/laguna-xs-2.1"],
      ["openrouter", "openrouter/free"]
    ]
  }
}`

const apiKeyForms = [
  { form: '!command', meaning: 'Runs the rest as a shell command and uses its trimmed stdout as the key.' },
  { form: 'env:VAR', meaning: 'Reads the environment variable VAR.' },
  { form: 'anything else', meaning: 'Treated as a literal key.' },
]

const envVars = [
  { variable: 'ABSTRACT_MODEL', overrides: 'model' },
  { variable: 'ABSTRACT_PROVIDER', overrides: 'provider' },
  { variable: 'ABSTRACT_EFFORT', overrides: 'effort' },
  { variable: 'ABSTRACT_THEME', overrides: 'theme' },
  { variable: 'ABSTRACT_MAX_TURNS', overrides: 'max_turns' },
  { variable: '<PROVIDER>_API_KEY', overrides: 'a provider key, via its env: spec' },
]
---

<Docs
  title="Configuration"
  description="Where the app's settings live: the in-app panes for everyday preferences, and the layered JSON config for the agent, sync accounts, and model providers."
  toc={toc}
>
  <Callout tone="tip" title="Nothing here is required">
    A local task list needs no configuration at all. The agent and the sync integrations are opt-in, and
    each one asks for credentials the first time you use it.
  </Callout>

  <h2 id="settings">In-app settings</h2>
  <p>
    Preferences are edited in the app rather than in a file. Each of these is a pane of its own:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Settings</strong> — application-level preferences.</li>
    <li><strong>Tag settings</strong> — per-tag behavior for the tag tree.</li>
    <li><strong>Integrations</strong> — the connected accounts: Todoist and GitHub.</li>
    <li><strong>Automations</strong> — the semi-automated workflows a task can carry.</li>
    <li><strong>Mini-apps</strong> — the panels that manage their own slice of your lists, such as travel checklists.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="agent">Agent providers and models</h2>
  <p>
    The agent pane and <code>agent-cli</code> share one configuration, a layered JSON file merged in this
    order — later wins:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>built-in defaults</li>
    <li><code>~/.abstract/config.json</code> — your global settings</li>
    <li><code>.abstract/config.json</code> — per-project settings</li>
    <li><code>ABSTRACT_*</code> environment variables</li>
    <li>CLI flags</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Providers are OpenAI-compatible and come with sensible defaults, so the common case is picking one and
    supplying a key. Override or add a provider under <code>providers</code>; only set the fields you want
    to change.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock filename=".abstract/config.json" code={config} />
  <p>An <code>api_key</code> takes one of three forms:</p>
  <TableScroll label="API key forms">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Form</th>
          <th>Meaning</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          apiKeyForms.map((entry) => (
            <tr>
              <td><code>{entry.form}</code></td>
              <td>{entry.meaning}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </TableScroll>
  <p>
    A <strong>combo</strong> is a named list of provider/model pairs that shows up in the model picker as a
    single choice. It runs on its first entry and, if that fails before producing any output (a provider
    error or a rate limit), retries on the next one. Because the retry only happens before any output,
    work is never duplicated.
  </p>
  <p>
    Environment variables override the file, which is handy for shells and CI:
  </p>
  <TableScroll label="Environment variables">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Variable</th>
          <th>Overrides</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          envVars.map((entry) => (
            <tr>
              <td><code>{entry.variable}</code></td>
              <td>{entry.overrides}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </TableScroll>
  <p>
    The complete provider, model, and environment-variable reference is in{' '}
    <code>apps/agent-cli/README.md</code>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="todoist">Todoist</h2>
  <p>
    Add your Todoist account in the integrations pane to turn on two-way sync. Once connected, the app
    imports your projects and tasks and keeps changes flowing in both directions; you keep working wherever
    you prefer, and the local database stays authoritative when the network is not there.
  </p>
  <p>
    How the mapping works, and exactly which fields are pushed today, is on the{' '}
    <a href="/docs/contributor/integrations#todoist">integrations page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="github">GitHub</h2>
  <p>
    GitHub issues and projects sync is in preview. <Badge tone="accent" variant="subtle">preview</Badge>{' '}
    Authenticate from the integrations pane; the app then maps issues and projects onto your lists, and the
    coding workflow can use a real checkout for its git-backed stages.
  </p>

  <h2 id="deeper">Going deeper</h2>
  <p>
    Tool servers, lifecycle hooks, and proxies are configured in the same JSON file — those, plus the Agent
    Client Protocol that connects the app to the agent, are documented on the{' '}
    <a href="/docs/contributor/integrations">integrations</a> page because they are closer to the internals than to a
    preference.
  </p>
</Docs>
